From 727dd3ead7b833f7579b5403ce1204c35c6d4c8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:03:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chat: tool_choice none keeps the none parser's plain replies
 and cuts rejected calls

Second review follow-up to 8120c3ced and 64a4084b3.

- Plain replies on reasoning templates started with blank lines under none:
  the none parsers drop the whitespace between the reasoning end tag and the
  content (p.space()), the auto parsers keep it as the separator before a
  call. The session now left-trims the content on the call-drop path when
  the reasoning is extracted (streaming-safe: it only ever extends a prefix).
  Hit DeepSeek V3.1, DeepSeek-R1-Distill, GLM-4.6/4.7-Flash, QwQ,
  Nemotron-Nano-v2, Spark2.5 and others.
- A call the auto parser rejects (unknown tool name, text after the call) fell
  back to the none parser's content, raw call included. The fallback now cuts
  that content at the first call opener; every opener passed the tag-like
  check, so the cut never lands in ordinary text.
- Ling 3 under tool_choice auto with tools offered returned `<|role_end|>` at
  the end of a reply with no call: the content ran to CALL_START only. It now
  ends at ROLE_END too, as the no-tools parser does (found by the sweep below).

Tests (tests/test-chat.cpp):
- the tool_choice none sweep now also takes every reply with no call, offers a
  tool, and requires exactly the template's own none parser output, streamed
  byte by byte through test_peg_parser (call cases were already streamed);
  disabling the left-trim fails it on QwQ;
- main fails unless the templates kept content-only are exactly
  command-r-plus, firefunction-v2 and functionary v3.2;
- Qwen3 and DeepSeek V3.1 cases for an unknown tool and for text after the
  call under none; disabling the cut fails them.

Verified CPU-only with Qwen3.5-0.8B-Q8_0 through llama-server: tool_choice
none returns plain text in stream on/off x thinking on/off and a plain reply
has no leading whitespace; auto still returns the call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BidfYiPxg2nUvGVowCgTPK
